														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2333495">
									

<p>The way it's used here is distinctly overdone and comes off as trying <em>really hard</em> to make sure we understand how they're related, for whatever reason.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Here's&nbsp;some&nbsp;feedback</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>CArgent: Ha ha, very funny, bro.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one's really blatant and sets the whole off on the wrong foot. You can lose it without losing anything at all.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>CArgent: What am I supposed to do, bro?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one's less unnecessary, but still, you could lose it without losing anything.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>RodArg: It's a hamster, sis. Give it a wheel.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one works, but could still be lost.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>CArgent: It's not a ham- …That's why you're the biologist and I'm the physicist. Thank you, bro.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sounds unnatural to me. You can get rid of it because the next one&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>RodArg: You're still the smart one with the promotion, sis. You're welcome.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;would give us all the information necessary if you left it in, without taking up the entire log with needless reminders that they're siblings.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

